cff-version: 1.2.0
title: "AAA — Accurate Autonomous Adaptation"
message: "If you refer to this work, please cite it as below."
type: software
authors:
  - name: "Cinqic"
repository-code: "https://github.com/Cinqic/AAA"
license: Apache-2.0
version: "0.2.0"
abstract: >-
  An experimental research prototype investigating whether an autonomous system
  can observe a small, inspectable environment, learn to predict what happens
  next, detect when its existing knowledge is no longer adequate, adapt from
  subsequent evidence, and improve its future predictions. The environment is
  deliberately small and the learner deliberately tiny; the emphasis is on a
  benchmark protocol capable of disproving the project's own hypotheses. No
  general-intelligence claim is made or supported.
keywords:
  - online learning
  - recursive least squares
  - adaptation
  - benchmark methodology
  - reproducibility
